---
// IPR: About and methodology. Replaces the theme's colophon. The standing text is written here
// on purpose; its substance follows the project's published methodology and doctrine.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/common/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../config';

const sections = [
  {
    id: 'what',
    title: 'What this is',
    body: [
      `${site.name} is an independent, source-grounded project that preserves and analyses official Indo-Pacific defense and security publication. It has two layers under one masthead: the record, an automated preservation of what official institutions publish, and Indo-Pacific Record Briefs, a human-controlled analytical collection.`,
      'Its readers are people who need to know what a government actually said and when: researchers, policy staff, analysts and journalists.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'preservation',
    title: 'Source preservation',
    body: [
      'Each item is collected from the institution that published it and stored as published. The original-language text is the authoritative record in every case.',
      'The collector identifies itself, respects robots.txt and does not defeat access challenges. A source that cannot be reached on those terms is recorded as blocked, not worked around.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'layers',
    title: 'Record, processing and analysis',
    body: [
      'Translation, summary and categorisation are model processing. They are labelled as automated and can be wrong. Items a model has flagged for attention are labelled model-flagged: a triage cue from software, not an editorial judgment.',
      'Analysis is human and labelled as such. In a brief, every claim traces to a source record, and inference is set apart from evidence.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'desks',
    title: 'Desks',
    body: [
      'Collection is organised by desk. China and Singapore are live desks, collecting into the public record. Other desks may collect privately in shadow while they are evaluated; a shadow desk is not promoted automatically and is not described as qualified until it has met the stated criteria and been signed off.',
      'Regional Security is an editorial grouping that reads across the collecting desks. The Archive desk points to the production record system.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'editorial',
    title: 'Editorial notes and corrections',
    body: [
      'Gaps in the record are recorded as warnings. They are not filled in from memory or from secondary reporting. Nothing is invented: not text, titles, dates, units, ranks or claims.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'limits',
    title: 'Limitations',
    body: [
      'The record can only hold what institutions publish. Official outlets do not report what their governments choose not to publicise, so the absence of coverage is a data point, not evidence that nothing happened.',
      'The record is only as wide as its live desks. Governments without a live desk are outside it, and briefs say so rather than filling the gap.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About & methodology"
  description={`What ${site.name} is, how the record is kept, and where it stops.`}
>
  <div class="max-w-content mx-auto px-4 pt-10 sm:pt-16">
    <PageHead
      title="About & methodology"
      lede="A source-linked record and analysis project focused on Indo-Pacific security, defense messaging, official records, and regional policy."
      folio="Prototype page · the full methodology is published on the production site"
    />

    {sections.map((section) => (
      <section class="mt-14 sm:mt-20" aria-labelledby={section.id}>
        <h2
          id={section.id}
          class="font-ui border-b border-current pb-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] uppercase"
        >
          {section.title}
        </h2>
        <div class="article-body mt-7">
          {section.body.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}

    <p class="mt-14 font-mono text-xs uppercase">
      <a class="hover:text-primary" href={`${site.recordUrl}/methodology.html`}>
        Full methodology on the production site ↗
      </a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
